  "limitations": [
    "The new decoder was selected after inspecting smaller development and diagnostic data; this is a post-deployment paired audit, not a preregistered release gate.",
    "Three variants per source are correlated; combined intervals resample complete document clusters within category.",
    "Exact reference matching can penalize acceptable alternative phrases.",
    "Balanced domains do not estimate this user's natural workload mix.",
    "Legacy and new timing runs were not interleaved; no causal latency claim from this comparison.",
    "MiniCPM legacy is the investigation baseline with the continuation-BOS fix; it was never the production default."
  ],
  "status": "Complete: both legacy HF models ran all 360 frozen cases without tuning, exclusions or failed requests.",
  "interpretation": [
    "Against legacy with the same model, Qwen improves by 2/360 and MiniCPM by 1/360. Both document-clustered confidence intervals include zero.",
    "Whole-input accuracy falls from 108 to 105 for Qwen and 105 to 103 for MiniCPM; gains concentrate in suffix/single-character inputs.",
    "The deployed MiniCPM native option scores 327/360 versus the retired Qwen legacy production baseline at 331/360. This changes both model and decoder.",
    "No demonstrated overall accuracy advantage; architecture correctness and native speed are separate claims."
  ],
